fact WorkItem(id: "WI-618", description: some(value: "Loader/parser: bare 'pattern -> body' (keyword-less lambda typo) is still SILENTLY accepted outside op/const bodies — empirically: a rule body '?y <=> ((x, acc) -> cons(head: x, tail: acc))' and a contract clause 'ensures all_match(result, (x) -> x > 0)' both load with ZERO diagnostics; the arrow term rides as inert data with unresolved-name leaves, so the rule/contract never means what was written (silent-skip, worse in kind than the loud op-body cascade WI-605 fixed). A blanket error is WRONG there (arrow-as-type is legitimate in term positions — types are terms), so the discriminator needs provenance, not context: mark pratt-minted '->'/'@' operator terms at desugar time (parse-side ParseAux flag or a minted-TermId set on ParsedFile) so consumers can tell the infix operator from a user-named 'arrow' functor exactly, then (a) flag arrow terms whose LEAVES are unresolved lowercase names in rule-body/contract term positions, (b) simplify WI-605's bare_arrow_lambda_suspect string+scope heuristic into an exact provenance check (per /code-review: every future pratt consumer — simp rewriting 043, scaland, reflect-as-data — otherwise re-implements the heuristic and drifts). Found by WI-605 /code-review (10-angle); empirical repros in the review transcript. ACCEPTANCE: rule-body and ensures/requires bare-arrow typos produce a loud diagnostic; legitimate arrow-type terms over resolved sorts still load; cargo-test green."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: ["WI-605"]), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-03T04:50:21Z"))

